body:
In the ui-v2 schema form, selecting a value in a required array field and then clearing it left `{ colors: [] }` in the form values. `[]` satisfies json schema's `required` check, so `/ui/schemas/validate` returned valid and a run was created with `colors: []` instead of erroring with `'colors' is a required property`.

`SchemaFormProperty` now emits `undefined` (which `SchemaFormInputObject` turns into a deleted key) when a required array value is shorter than its minimum, where a required array without an explicit `minItems` is treated as `minItems: 1`:

```ts
const arrayProperty = /* the matching anyOf branch, if any */;
const minItems = typeof arrayProperty.minItems === "number" ? arrayProperty.minItems : 1;
return value.length < minItems;
```

Consequences:

- optional arrays keep sending `[]`, so a stored default can still be cleared;
- required arrays with an explicit `minItems: 0` (e.g. block fields that legitimately accept an empty list) also keep sending `[]`, so schemas can opt out;
- the normalization also runs on incoming values and on default initialization, so a required field that starts out as `[]` is omitted too;
- the input keeps its own `internalValue`, so the field still renders as emptied while the error shows.

Tests in `schema-form-input-array-enum.test.tsx` and `schema-form-input-enum.test.tsx` cover these cases.

Closes https://github.com/PrefectHQ/prefect/issues/22746

